name: sim.packUInt32Table
description: Packs an array of uint32 numbers into a string
luaSynopsis: bytes data = sim.packUInt32Table(list uint32Numbers, int startUint32Index = 0, int uint32Count = 0)
pythonSynopsis: buffer data = sim.packUInt32Table(int[] uint32Numbers, int startUint32Index = 0, int uint32Count = 0)
inputs:
1. uint32Numbers: array containing uint32 numbers. Non-numbers will be packed as zero values
2. startUint32Index: zero-based index from which on data should be packed. Can be omitted in which case 0 is used
3. uint32Count: amount of uint32s that should be packed. Can be omitted in which case 0 is used (which indicates that the maximum available uint32s should be packed from the indicated startUint32Index)
outputs:
1. data: a buffer (values between 0 and 255) that contains packed uint32 numbers
replacedBy:
- name: packArray, class: app, file: app_packArray.method
